rationale:
**1. Structure: three pains, each paired with its answer, interleaved and readable muted.**

| Pain | Answer |
|---|---|
| « Votre salon, encore au carnet ? » | « Votre journée, heure par heure. » (Ma journée) |
| « Encore les mêmes questions ? » (price, where, hours, at 22:41–23:02) | « Tarifs, horaires, plan : tout sur votre page. » (public page) |
| « Un client sans rendez-vous ? » (squeezed into the notebook, no number) | « En quelques gestes, même sans numéro. » (Libre — 14:45 → Client sans numéro → Rendez-vous créé) |

The film opens and closes inside « Ma journée », and the S6 notebook's 14h / 14h45 / 15h30 rhymes with the real agenda's 14:00 / Libre — 14:45 / 15:30.

**2. Timing.** Cuts fall at 2.5 / 6.0 / 10.0 / 12.5 / 17.5 / 20.0 / 26.5 s (frames 75 / 180 / 300 / 375 / 525 / 600 / 795), all on a 0.5 s (120 BPM) grid. Pain beats get 2.5 s each, as the marketing judge asked; answers get 4.0 / 5.0 / 6.5 s; the end card gets 3.5 s.

**3. Reading times.** The rule is: on screen from the start of the entrance to the start of the exit ≥ max(1.5 s, characters ÷ 15 + 0.5 s).

| Text | On screen | Needed |
|---|---|---|
| S1 headline | 2.70 s | 2.57 s |
| S2 tagline | 2.80 s | 2.77 s |
| S3 | 3.80 s | 2.57 s |
| S4 | 2.70 s | 2.37 s |
| S5 | 4.75 s | 3.57 s |
| S6 | 2.68 s | 2.37 s |
| S7 | 6.05 s | 2.97 s |
| CTA | 2.60 s | 2.23 s |

I measured every line with the repo's Poppins-Medium.ttf and Inter-Variable.ttf. Every headline line is ≤ 900 px; pain lines are 92 px and answer lines 84 px, because 88 px pushed « Tarifs, horaires, plan : » to 926 px and « même sans numéro. » to 919 px.

**4. Meta's correlates, met without hype:**
- the hook works at frame 0;
- brand plus main promise land at 2.7–3.5 s;
- the brand is shown twice, for 23.3% of the runtime;
- the product is shown in three answers on four real screens;
- a concrete feature is shown in every answer;
- the CTA is on screen.

**5. Judges' fixes applied:**
- **Camera window.** It crops each capture from screen point 56, so neither the status bar nor the Dynamic Island ever shows.
- **S3.** It now ends on the open « Arrivé » pane; the tap and the 1.3 s wait are gone.
- **No-show pair replaced.** The weak « lapin » / « 0 Absences » pair is gone.
- **Public page.** S5 shows only the public page, under wording that is literal on screen (« Voir les tarifs », map, hours). The 'place' bubble is gone.
- **Tagline.** It moves next to the logo inside the first 5 s.
- **Discs.** A white disc on the black « Créer » button.
- **Arrows.** Set in Inter, because Poppins-Medium.ttf has no U+2192; I checked it renders the notdef box.
- **Small text.** Notebook and bubble text is now 48 px, and timestamps are 34 px #8A8A8A (4.8:1).
- **Gone from the film:** the S8 stills that went past the safe margin, the stale Revenus and Accueil captures, the unverified cover photo, and every client phone number. The only phone on screen is the masked salon row in S5.

**6. Brand.**
- Ink Black and paper only. The only functional colours are inside the real UI (the green « Arrivé » pane and the « Rendez-vous créé » snackbar).
- Poppins Medium and Inter, at most two weights per screen, no italics.
- The motion tokens throughout: stagger 50, fast 100, base 200, emphasis 300, slow 400. Entrances decelerate, exits accelerate, and the Lottie's (0.4, 0, 0.2, 1) is used for every stroke.
- The logo exists only as SVG and Lottie vectors, and its clear space (half the mark's height) is kept.

**7. Build (Python, Pillow and numpy, plus AVFoundation; no ffmpeg).**
- **Encoder.** A new MovieSpec.social: 1080×1920, 30 fps, 900 frames, H.264 High@4.1, about 12 Mbps, a keyframe every 30 frames, and a silent stereo AAC 48 kHz track (safe for the IG, Facebook, TikTok and WhatsApp uploaders). writeMovie and the 1080×1920 encode were already probe-tested in the brief.
- **Footage.**
  - take1b: four LIVE and HOLD ranges conformed with Conform.swift (10.662–11.628, 32.165–33.032, 130.262–132.195, plus the holds).
  - take5b at 30.000 s: one frame, grabbed at zero tolerance. A working grabber is in the scratchpad: final-sb/grab.swift.
- **Compositor primitives:**
  - a trimmed polyline stroke for the mark, with round caps and joins, supersampled;
  - a stroke that thickens into a full-frame fill;
  - the Seyès field;
  - chat bubbles with a slot stack;
  - text pop, rise and stagger;
  - a card with camera window W(t), the mask applied in capture space before scaling, and shadows;
  - the touch disc;
  - the brand pattern;
  - the squircle icon tile;
  - the wordmark unit through rsvg-convert, with the « Pro » glyph paths extracted from the Lottie.
- **Curve.** Add CUBICS 'fastOutSlowIn' = (0.4, 0, 0.2, 1).
- **Verify must check:**
  - 1080×1920, 900 frames, exactly 30.000 fps;
  - no notdef glyph in any rendered string;
  - the take5b phone rect is fully covered on every S5 frame, including during the camera moves;
  - all film text sits inside x 65–1015 and y 269–1248;
  - the reading-time table and brand time ≤ 25%;
  - each LIVE and HOLD range against its take map.

**8. Deliverables from one master:**
- master.mp4;
- cover.png (frame 51, 1.70 s);
- a contact sheet;
- verify.txt;
- a cut-down (S1 + S2 + S3 + end card = 13.5 s, the « carnet → Ma journée » story).

**9. Suggested post caption** (not part of the video, under 44 characters): « Le carnet, c’est fini. Essayez MyWeli Pro. » (41 characters).

Because Instagram reaches about 0.9M people in Côte d'Ivoire against about 8.4M on Facebook, post the same master to Facebook Reels, TikTok and WhatsApp Status as well.

